# The lockfile must stay portable: `package-lock.json` records every
# `resolved` URL, and `npm ci` fetches exactly those — `npm config set registry`
# and `NPM_CONFIG_REGISTRY` do NOT rewrite them for lockfileVersion 3. Pinning a
# mirror here once baked `registry.npmmirror.com` into all 899 entries, which
# made the build impossible on any machine that cannot reach that host and left
# "change the registry" as the only fix nobody could apply (issue #212).
#
# So: the official registry, so a freshly generated lock stays official.
# Acceleration belongs to the machine, not the repository — set it in
# ~/.npmrc or per-run, e.g.
#   npm ci --registry=https://registry.npmmirror.com
# CI enforces the lockfile half of this (tests/lockfile-registry.test.ts, and
# the `lockfile-registry` job in .github/workflows/pr.yml).
registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/
